<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Data Sources</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We integrate data from four sources: MIMIC-CXR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Johnson et al., 2019</a>)</cite> for images and reports, Chest ImaGenome <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2021</a>)</cite> for labeled organs and diseases, and both MIMIC-CXR-VQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bae et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and Medical-Diff-VQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2023</a>)</cite> for QA pairs involving single and comparative images. Below are brief descriptions of each dataset:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MIMIC-CXR (v2.0.0)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Johnson et al., 2019</a>)</cite> is a large-scale, publicly available dataset containing 377,110 chest radiographs with structured labels derived from 227,827 free-text radiology reports, collected at BIDMC between 2011 and 2016.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Chest ImaGenome (v1.0.0)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2021</a>)</cite> provides scene graph annotations for 242,072 frontal chest X-rays from MIMIC-CXR, explicitly representing anatomical locations and their associated attributes. It comprises two subsets: the automatically generated silver dataset covering all images, and the clinician-validated gold dataset derived from 500 unique patients.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MIMIC-CXR-VQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bae et al., 2023</a>)</cite> is a medical visual question answering dataset containing approximately 377,000 QA pairs associated with chest X-rays. This dataset was constructed by integrating MIMIC-CXR, MIMIC-IV <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Johnson et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and Chest ImaGenome. It includes 48 unique question templates categorized into seven clinical domains: existence, anatomy, attribute, abnormality, size, plane, and gender. Each template provides approximately 16.5 paraphrases generated by GPT-4 under clinical expert guidance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Medical-Diff-VQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2023</a>)</cite> is a medical difference visual question answering dataset, constructed from MIMIC-CXR. It contains 700,703 QA pairs from 164,324 image pairs, organized into seven clinically relevant categories: abnormality, location, type, level, view, presence, and difference. It involves chest radiograph comparisons to support comparative clinical reasoning aligned with standard medical practices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">All the above datasets are publicly available on PhysioNet platform <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">PhysioNet, [n. d.]</a>)</cite>, requiring credentialed access approval.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Data Statistics</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides a detailed statistical overview of the datasets used for training and evaluation. The key aspects of the dataset statistics include the number of samples for different subtasks, the distribution of training, validation, and test sets, and the ratio of closed and open-ended questions in each dataset. Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix B Data Statistics ‣ CheXPO: Preference Optimization for Chest X-ray VLMs with Counterfactual Rationale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> outlines the key dataset statistics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The MIMIC-CXR-VQA<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bae et al., 2023</a>)</cite> dataset provides seven distinct question types: <span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Presence</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Anatomy</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Attribute</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Abnormality</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Size</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Plane</span>, and <span id="A2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gender</span>. The Medical-Diff-VQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2023</a>)</cite> dataset, while also offering seven question types, has some differences compared to MIMIC-CXR-VQA. The question types in this dataset include <span id="A2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Abnormality</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Presence</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">View</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Location</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Severity</span>, <span id="A2.p2.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Type</span>, and <span id="A2.p2.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Difference</span>. Given the overlap between some categories, such as <span id="A2.p2.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Location</span> and <span id="A2.p2.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Anatomy</span>, and <span id="A2.p2.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">View</span> and <span id="A2.p2.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Plane</span>, these types have been merged in the final classification, resulting in ten distinct categories overall, as shown in Figure <a href="#A2.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix B Data Statistics ‣ CheXPO: Preference Optimization for Chest X-ray VLMs with Counterfactual Rationale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. The aligned question types and their corresponding examples are summarized in Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Data Statistics ‣ CheXPO: Preference Optimization for Chest X-ray VLMs with Counterfactual Rationale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
